<00:00:00.154>But <00:00:00.219>I <00:00:00.273>saw <00:00:00.458>something <00:00:00.719>she <00:00:00.849>could <00:00:00.980>not. <00:00:01.654>One <00:00:01.860>winter <00:00:02.132>morning, <00:00:02.697>the <00:00:02.773>ground <00:00:03.089>around <00:00:03.393>me <00:00:03.523>was <00:00:03.665>white. <00:00:04.360>A <00:00:04.436>thin <00:00:04.741>coat <00:00:04.980>of <00:00:05.067>frost <00:00:05.491>had <00:00:05.610>formed <00:00:05.980>on <00:00:06.056>the <00:00:06.121>rocks. <00:00:06.947>Water <00:00:07.219>ice, <00:00:07.730>on <00:00:07.871>Mars, <00:00:08.545>right <00:00:08.686>in <00:00:08.763>front <00:00:08.926>of <00:00:08.969>my <00:00:09.089>cameras.

